# Purpose
Shows users how to start, join, co-edit, send, and leave a Tandem Turns
session in the dashboard console.

# Key Sections
- What a session is (same-node, one per node, short-lived, send ends it).
- Start or join via the TT button; controller accept/reject.
- Co-editing: avatar strip, live merge, gold border, four-person cap.
- Send: confirmation overlay, one turn for the group, everyone exits TT mode.
- Leave and troubleshooting.

# Dependencies
- `use-console-main-row-and-prompt-controls.md`
- `../concepts/what-is-a-node.md`

# Gotchas
- Keep the locked semantics exact: same-node only, one session per node,
  send ends the session for everyone, and a recovery-window miss preserves
  the local draft while exiting TT for manual reconciliation.
- Public-safe: no protocol frame names, file paths, or internal repo names.

# Change History
- 2026-08-31b: Same-user multi-device — your own devices join instantly with
  no approval, share one colour, and inherit control if the creating device
  goes away; node-switch TT click now starts/joins on the new node.
- 2026-08-31: Created for the Tandem Turns v1 browser release.
